[2026-09-03T17:01:56Z] FIXED double-click issue (models/index.js + library/index.js): (1) refreshModels serialized so overlapping 2s refreshes (slow /api/models probing remotes) can't stack+race on innerHTML; (2) DOM swap skipped when payload unchanged; (3) press-tracking defers the swap until after click dispatch. VERIFIED: 8/8 clicks landed across a refresh tick
[2026-09-03T17:09:15Z] FIXED log auto-scroll bug (models/index.js updateLogPanel): textContent reset scrollTop to 0 before the pinned check, yanking the panel to top on every update. Now captures wasPinned + prevScrollTop BEFORE replacing text and restores position (bottom if pinned, previous position otherwise). VERIFIED via isolated DOM test
[2026-09-03T17:20:44Z] FIXED loading overlay lingering on crash (models/index.js waitForSpawn): now tracks whether the server ever transitioned to starting/online; if it returns to offline (crash) it bails immediately, clearing inFlight so the blur/spinner disappears right away instead of waiting the full 5s poll window. VERIFIED via isolated test (bailed on poll 3)
[2026-09-03T18:01:12Z] ADDED per-GPU VRAM tracking (main.py + gpu.py + system/index.js + index.html + styles.css): each GPU gets its own graph + toggle; untracked GPUs (e.g. iGPU) are excluded from the aggregate total; tracked state persisted in .metallama_gpu_config.json (excluded_gpus list, default = all tracked). New endpoints: GET /api/system/vram/gpus, POST /api/system/vram/gpus/toggle; /api/system/vram/history now returns per-GPU history under 'gpus'. Also FIXED gpu.py tool detection under systemd's restricted PATH (venv-only): added absolute-path fallbacks for rocm-smi/amd-smi and made query functions use the resolved tool path. VERIFIED end-to-end in browser: toggle card2 off drops aggregate 48.5→48.0 GB, persists across reload, re-enable restores.
[2026-09-03T18:13:23Z] UPDATED VRAM UI (index.html + system/index.js + styles.css): total graph now shown first; individual GPU cards moved below a collapsible "Individual GPUs" separator (persisted in localStorage, metallama.gpusSectionOpen); untracked GPUs are dimmed, moved to the bottom of the list, and their graph is hidden. VERIFIED in browser: collapse/expand persists, untracked card2 moves to bottom with graph hidden, aggregate still only sums tracked GPUs.
[2026-09-03T18:30:04Z] UPDATED main.py — the aggregate VRAM total graph is now computed on-demand from per-GPU histories of currently-tracked GPUs (aligned by timestamp), instead of being stored at probe time. Untracking a GPU now also removes its past data from the total graph. Removed the now-unused vram_history deque. VERIFIED: card2 off drops total 48.46→47.96, re-enable restores 48.46.
